# Shell scripts must check out with LF on every platform.
#
# This repo had no .gitattributes, so line endings were left to whatever
# core.autocrlf each machine happened to have. Git for Windows defaults it to
# `true`, which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout — and a trailing \r is a syntax
# error to bash, not whitespace. Measured on a Windows checkout 2026-08-13:
#
#   bash _harness/sync.sh
#   : invalid option: line 9: set: -            <- `set -e\r`
#   line 10: cd: $'_harness/..\r': No such file or directory
#   line 69: syntax error near unexpected token `$'do\r''
#
# The mirror was never built and the harness could not run at all. The blobs
# are stored LF and always were; only the working copy was mangled, which is
# why it reproduced on one machine and not another.
#
# Both scripts carry a shebang and are executed by a POSIX shell — sync.sh
# directly, fakemail.sh through PHP's sendmail_path — so both need LF.
*.sh text eol=lf
